{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"dripping-captious-arctichare","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\nThe src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler cohort contains audited comments or docstrings that obscure current behavior with repetition, obvious narration, duplicated explanation, or historical detail. The audit is pinned to `9e65567b79ffe872534c3c656ade7b34340d8192`.\n\n## Approach\nEdit explanatory text only in this directory/subsystem cohort. Condense it to current, non-obvious rationale and constraints; retain every file-specific preserve item and consumer contract below. Grouping adjacent files from one subsystem keeps the change reviewable in one session and permits one coherent verification pass without changing executable behavior.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/mutation_payloads.py:1-34, 429-435, 466-473` — Preserve the closed typed-payload mapping and rejection behavior. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_comments.py:1-65, 88-109, 130-172, 203-280, 309-344, 379-440, 463-515, 534-537, 562-633, 671-722` — Preserve marker-safe fitting, ID/body dedup, live-fetch decisions, breadcrumb handling, and convergence. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_differ.py:1-20, 31-37, 71-115, 161-195, 236-341, 353-359, 396-433, 463-521, 544-576, 626-644` — Preserve authoritative absence checks, arbitration, enrichment, and mutation planning. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_effective_maps.py:1-17, 30-39, 51-58, 77-85, 101-109, 128-135, 154-166, 189-195` — Preserve effective per-project map resolution and map-or-drift/default behavior. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_re